          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The Łoś
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultraproduct"} ultraproduct
            theorem characterizes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order theory
            of an ultraproduct of
            = succeed "-structures" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
            some
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+%28in+logic%29"} signature
            %em transfer principle
            from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonstandard+analysis"} nonstandard analysis
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo
                    %mo *
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^*\mathbb{R}
            with an ultraproduct and formulas from the standard reals
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            with formulas which are true on an “ultrafilter-large” subset of factors of the ultraproduct.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p The theorem is usually given in this form:
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_i)_{i \in I}
              be a family of nonempty
              = succeed "-structures," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultrafilter"} ultrafilter
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^* A
              be the ultraproduct of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i
              with respect to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i
              was nonempty,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^* A
              is the quotient of the product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{i \in I} A_i
              by the equivalence relation which identifies sequences which coincide on a subset of indices belonging to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_i)_{i \in I}
              be such a sequence, and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [(a_i)]
              denote its equivalence class. Then for each
              = succeed "-formula" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi(x)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊧
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi j
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo ⊧
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^* A \models \varphi([a_i]) \iff \{j \in I | A_j \models \varphi(a_j)\} \in \mathcal{U}.
          %p The above follows from a more fundamental fact:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p Any functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Set
                      %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{U}] : \mathbf{Set}^I \to \mathbf{Set}
            %p
              which specifies a choice of ultraproduct (and hence comparison maps, since ultraproducts are colimits) is elementary (logical in the terminology of Makkai-Reyes, i.e. a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
              morphism.)
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Recall that the ultraproduct sends the family of sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i
              to the colimit of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ↦
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \mapsto \prod_{i \in s} A_i
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi U
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in U^op
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^op
              (the opposite category of the sub-poset
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq \mathcal{P}(I)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is a filter.
            %p A functor is a pretopos morphism precisely when it preserves finite limits, initial objects, disjoint sums, and quotients by internal equivalence relations.
            %p
              Finite limits: a
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            %p
              Initial objects: a
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              is nonempty by properness of
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %p
              Disjoint sums: a
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mi i
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{i:s} (A_{0i} + A_{1i})
              is a disjoint sum of products
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo :
                          %mi s
                          %mo →
                          %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo :
                          %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{f : s \to 2} \prod_{i:s} A_{f(i)i}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,a)
              in this set, there is a
              = succeed "-large" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \subset s
              such that the restriction of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              is constantly
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in \{0,1\}
              ). Therefore the restriction map identifies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,a)
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi const
                        %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (const_b,a|_t)
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi U
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^op
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi s
                        %mo →
                        %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{f : s \to 2} \prod_{i:s} A_{f(i)i}
              is equivalent to the
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi U
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^op
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                          %mo :
                          %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo :
                          %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi bi
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo :
                          %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo :
                          %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{b : 2} \prod_{i:s} A_{bi} = \prod_{i:s} A_{0i} + \prod_{i:s} A_{1i}
            %p
              Quotients: Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
              and equivalence relations
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_i \to X_i \times X_i
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{i:s} (X_i / E_i)
              is a quotient of products
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\prod_{i:s} X_i) / (\prod_{i:s} E_i)
              (because the natural map from the latter to the former is an iso, using the axiom of choice), and colimits commute with colimits.
          %p Now we can show the theorem:
          .proof
            %h6#proof_of_theorem Proof of theorem
            %p
              Since the ultraproduct functor is elementary, then the process of taking points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M(X)
              of a definable set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              inside models
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              commutes with taking ultraproducts. In symbols,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mo )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mo )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\prod_{i \in I} M_i / \mathcal{U}\right) (X) \simeq \left(\prod_{i \in I} M_i(X) / \mathcal{U}\right).
            %p
              Since this is a filtered colimit, a sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi x
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{x}
              satisfies that its germ
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mover
                      %mi x
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\overline{x}]
              is in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{i \in I} M_i / \mathcal{U}(X)
              if and only if there is some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \in \mathcal{U}
              such that the restriction of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi x
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{x}
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi J
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{j \in J} M_j(X)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi j
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_j \in M_j(X)
              for each
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \in J
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            An immediate consequence of the Łoś theorem is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonstandard+analysis"} transfer principle
            for the hyperreals.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactness+theorem"} compactness theorem
            also follows quickly from the Łoś theorem, so anything that you
            %a{:href => "http://math.stackexchange.com/questions/413770/most-astonishing-applications-of-compactness-theorem-outside-logic"} build
            using compactness can be realized a bit more concretely as an ultraproduct.
          %h2#remarks Remarks
          %p
            The proposition should be interpreted as saying that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            simultaneously carries a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
            structure and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultracategory"} ultracategory
            structure, and that these two structures commute. Indeed, one can view
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizing+object"} dualizing object
            for a generalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+duality"} Stone duality
            between pretoposes and ultracategories; this is the starting point of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Makkai+duality"} Makkai duality
          %p
            There is an analogous statement for ultraproducts of structures in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+logic"} continuous logic
